I still have this problem while using fastify 3.29.0:
```ts
 const errorHandler = async (error: Error, req, res) {
   console.error(error)
 }
  
fastify(options)
  .setErrorHandler(errorHandler)
  .delete("/:userId", {
      preHandler: async (req, res) => {
        throw new Error()
      },
      handler: async (req, res) => {
         ...
      })

```
When the `Error` is raised, `errorHandler` is *not* called. Instead it ends up with a 500.
